Package: rpi-power-profiles
Version: 1.0.2
Architecture: all
Maintainer: KRubus Project <https://github.com/GamingTux/KRubus>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/GamingTux/KRubus
Depends: python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, iw, systemd
Provides: power-profiles-daemon
Conflicts: power-profiles-daemon, argon-oneup-power-profiles
Replaces: power-profiles-daemon
Description: Generic Hardware Power Profiles Daemon for Raspberry Pi 5 & CM5
 Lightweight, event-driven drop-in replacement for power-profiles-daemon on
 Raspberry Pi 5, Pi 500, and Compute Module 5 (BCM2712 / Cortex-A76), where
 upstream power-profiles-daemon only exposes a non-functional placeholder.
 .
 Exports standard org.freedesktop.UPower.PowerProfiles and net.hadess.PowerProfiles
 D-Bus APIs for KDE Plasma 6 (PowerDevil), GNOME, GameMode, and powerprofilesctl:
  - power-saver: powersave governor (1.5 GHz min voltage), Wi-Fi powersave on,
    PCIe ASPM powersave, workqueue power_efficient=Y, 15s VFS writeback
  - balanced: schedutil governor (0.5 ms ramp-up to max/OC clock), Wi-Fi
    powersave off, PCIe ASPM default, workqueue power_efficient=Y
  - performance: performance governor (all 4 Cortex-A76 cores locked at max/OC
    clock), Wi-Fi powersave off, PCIe ASPM performance, workqueue power_efficient=N
